[TEXT] All evidence is in. The picture is complete.

- `router_core_3`'s OSPF neighbour table shows **only two peers** (router_core_1 and router_core_2). There is **no adjacency with `switch_server_access`**.
- `switch_server_access` has `eth5 172.16.0.11/31` (the uplink to router_core_3) and `br0 10.200.0.1/24` (the gateway for every server), but its **FRR running config is entirely empty** — no `router ospf`, no `network` statements, nothing.
- Every other FRR device has a correct OSPF stanza; only `switch_server_access` is dark.
- As a result, `10.200.0.0/24` is never injected into OSPF, and no core or distribution router has any route to it.

